# --- Program locks (see ProgramLock/PlatformLockState below): the
# single platform-wide Lock All / Unlock All switch. Everything is
# UNLOCKED by default (all_locked=False, every ProgramLock/
# PlatformFeatureFlag row starts unlocked — see _seed_feature_flag and
# register_program_locks). Once a platform admin locks something —
# one program, one feature flag, or Lock All — it stays truly locked,
# enforced on every request server-side (see _emergency_lock_gate
# below), until a platform admin explicitly unlocks it again. This is
# hardcoded on (not an environment variable) on purpose: an env var
# left over from an earlier deploy could silently disable enforcement
# again and reintroduce the exact "unlock says unlocked but it's still
# locked" bug this was fixed for.
